// @@@ If the index is valid (between 0 and the size of the set inclusive), then for every valid index up to the specified index, each element at that index either remains null if it was initially null, or remains unchanged compared to its initial state.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is within the valid range (from 0 to the size of the set), then for every valid index up to the specified index, either the element at that position is null and was null before, or it remains unchanged from its previous state.
--------------------
// @@@ If the index is between 0 and the size of the set inclusive, then for every index i from 0 to this index, the element at i is either null and was null before, or remains unchanged from its previous state.
